This file marks an installed copy of TrailMQ.

The launcher reads it to decide where your data belongs. When it is present,
TrailMQ keeps certificates, credentials, databases and logs under your own
user profile instead of writing into the program directory, which an
installation must never do.

Deleting this file turns the installation back into a portable copy, and the
launcher will then look for your data next to the program files, where it is
not. Leave it alone unless that is what you intend.
